From 876a2e7e1dfd901d34517749513b8b9d01083a07 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Mon, 18 May 2026 22:03:55 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] perf phase 11 patch 0160 -- SFX-stall instrumentation
 (486-campaign Bug 1, parts A + B-1)

486-class campaign Bug 1: every sound-effect trigger causes a
~0.3-0.45 s flip hitch, on all three 486 configs including the fastest
(Am5x86) -- the long-standing 0.1.0 "audio chop in effect-heavy scenes"
issue. The campaign could quantify the hitch but not place it: the
phase-timing had no per-SFX-trigger marker, and the engine-thread
audio-servicing call (runFade) fell into the un-bracketed "misc"
remainder of the audio/engine split. This patch adds the engine-side
instrumentation to localize the stall on the next real-HW run, per
docs/internal/SFX-STALL-INSTRUMENTATION-CONTRACT.md. Instrumentation
only -- no behavior change.

Part A -- per-SFX-trigger marker. SfxTriggerTimer (diagnostic_timers.h)
brackets SoundManager::playSfx / playSfxResampled, recording each
trigger's wall-clock call duration, the SFX id, and the flip it fired
on. Records accumulate in a per-100-flip block (a 256-entry call_us
sample array + the worst trigger's flip/id); _maybe_flush_sfx_stat_audit
emits one [sfx-stat block=N triggers=T call_us min/med/p95/max
busiest_flip=F max_sfx_id=ID] line per block. A large call_us places
the hitch inside the trigger call (Pixtone::play's synchronous
SDL_AudioStream create + resample); a small call_us with a slow
same/next flip places it downstream.

Part B-1 -- the audio-service bucket. AudioServiceTimer brackets
SoundManager::runFade() at its run_tick / run_tick_fixed call sites and
accumulates audio_service_*; _maybe_flush_audio_engine_split_audit emits
audio_service_ms_x10 alongside the existing audio_mixer / engine_tick
fields. This carves the last engine-thread audio call out of the
derived "misc" remainder. Every pre-0160 field keeps its name and
relative order, so the existing parse is preserved.

Part B-2 -- no engine hunk. The contract asked to bracket a Pixtone/SFX
stream callback if one exists engine-side. It does not: Pixtone drives
SFX through SDL3_mixer's MIX_* track pool; the only Pixtone-side
callback is a MIX_TrackStoppedCallback (fires on track completion, not
per-mix). The SFX mix runs inside SDL3_mixer + the SDL-DOS audio
callback -- SDL-side. Part C (sdl-engine) covers it.

All hooks gate on the existing cached FINE_INSTR bool
(engine_tick_fine_instr_active(), SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_FINE_INSTR). No new
env var. No boot banner. With FINE_INSTR=0 the SfxTriggerTimer /
AudioServiceTimer constructors take no SDL_GetTicksNS reading and record
nothing, the block counts stay 0, and the emits early-return -- the
FINE_INSTR=0 path is a behavioral no-op, byte-identical in behavior to
v1.0.0. Aggregation is once per 100-flip block (no per-trigger fsync,
no per-trigger getenv), matching the wave-58 [ft-accum-stat] pattern.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>
